                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "disperse",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "58d5edc8-3820-310f-ac8a-922a2642da19",
                                        "entry_id": "2a43456e-1b62-3345-9f1d-150661a323f4",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Scattered or spread out."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6350dc51-7def-40b8-b0a8-b4c08fd7b947",
                                                "sense_id": "58d5edc8-3820-310f-ac8a-922a2642da19",
                                                "text": "Australia itself is a very wide and very disperse country, where the distance problems significantly affect also the \"internal\" customer-supplier chains."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "dafc144d-c36c-498e-9255-b0d01030a68a",
                                                "sense_id": "58d5edc8-3820-310f-ac8a-922a2642da19",
                                                "text": "In particular, a very crisp quantifier such as “for all,” “there exists,” “at least 50 percent” tend to have less disperse weighting vectors while fuzzier quantifiers such as many tend to have a more disperse weighting vector."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "72d032b4-2f66-4bc1-90fb-bc114059398d",
                        "source_entry_id": "908be6ac-9d71-3c6c-bbdd-6eb3fb9009a3",
                        "source_sense_description": "связанный, соотносящийся по значению с существительным «дисперсия»",
                        "target_lang_word": "dispersed",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "dispersed",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "292cad93-49cf-371a-b42a-e2ba9f41fa9f",
                                        "entry_id": "6f3b3e75-998a-3218-8367-9b0b31bce20b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Spread out in space and/or time; not concentrated."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f7eea02d-8a06-4863-b1fa-460608357c04",
                                                "sense_id": "292cad93-49cf-371a-b42a-e2ba9f41fa9f",
                                                "text": "One other problem studied relates to the potential impact of human waste disposal from dispersed road recreation -- a matter of concern to many managers we've talked to ."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5ea081d8-0795-48f4-8301-838b0e21070e",
                                                "sense_id": "292cad93-49cf-371a-b42a-e2ba9f41fa9f",
                                                "text": "Practised in the context of a social movement, dispersed leadership has opened opportunities for women to adopt feminalist styles of leadership that invite and increase the participation of women as a group, while it has also provided the means to advance feminist agendas."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "624738a6-3810-4f2a-9101-efd9483dbedc",
                                                "sense_id": "292cad93-49cf-371a-b42a-e2ba9f41fa9f",
                                                "text": "On the contrary, a very dispersed and scarce one such as gold, will have a low exergy value but a very high extraction cost."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
